  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental activities only; no business-type funds. Receipts/disbursements/transfers from Exhibit D (p4) Total Governmental column; transfers in and out both 1,797,860 and cross-check by fund (General out 1,793,444 + Road out 4,416; Road in 749,344 + Self Insurance 1,044,100 + nonmajor 4,416); no hidden transfers. ending_cash 9,852,838 is the fund balance total which includes 70,331 designated investments (Horse Arena), so investments are not shown separately. Attempt 2 (2026-10-28 re-check): balance sheet now taken from Exhibit C Balance Sheet - Cash Basis, Governmental Funds (p3), Total column, with fund balance by classification (Restricted 1,099,339, Assigned 8,120,048, Unassigned 633,451), because its totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (Exhibit A p1: same assets 9,782,507 + 70,331 = 9,852,838; net position restricted by purpose 1,099,339 + unrestricted 8,753,499). No liabilities printed, total_liabilities null. Intergovernmental 2,115,636 is not broken down anywhere in the report (no homestead/property tax credit/pro-rate lines), so it stays state aid. Detail: General Fund, Road, Self Insurance and Inheritance Tax budget schedules (Exhibits F-I) plus Schedule 2 total column for nonmajor funds (more than 6 funds); Schedule 4 and Schedule 5 not itemized again to avoid double counting (Schedule 4 is a subset of Schedule 2 and Schedule 5 prints only fund totals). Blank actual cells recorded as 0 with printed budget. General Fund Taxes split into property and motor vehicle using Exhibit D General column (sum equals 4,093,699). Attempt 3 (charges-for-services re-check): budget schedules print only broad groups, so 'Local' lines are not split. Road Fund Local 61,313 moved to other (Exhibit D Road column: miscellaneous 32,373 is more than half; charges 28,645). General Fund Local 1,083,417 stays charges for services as the largest part (charges 499,345 vs interest 491,444; neither more than half), review names the mix. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
